      "message": "Hey Arthur,\nIn general, when you land a CL in Skia, you want to be watching this page:\n   https://status.skia.org/?filter\u003dInteresting\u0026repo\u003dskia\nIn this case, since your CL was reverted, the status page is hiding the failures so you need to click the \"Failures\" button in the top toolbar. This will take you to:\n   https://status.skia.org/?filter\u003dFailures\u0026repo\u003dskia\nIf you change the number of displayed CLs (in the upper-left hand corner \"Commits:\" box) then scroll down to the row for your CL you can see all the failing jobs.\nHere is a representative log:\n   https://logs.chromium.org/logs/skia/6bf3cdf9a4611911/+/steps/gn_gen/0/stdout\nIt seems to have hit a cross section of the Graphite_Dawn jobs on Linux and Windows.",
